WEBVTT

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:31.409
Recorded speaker 1:
I'm going to talk a little bit

00:03:31.433 --> 00:03:32.963
about the power of authenticity.

00:03:32.987 --> 00:03:35.804
Recorded speaker 2: I was asked
to speak about authenticity.

00:03:35.828 --> 00:03:38.939
AG: It kind of feels like we're living
in the age of authenticity.

00:03:38.963 --> 00:03:40.878
Recorded speaker 3: I'm here to tell you

00:03:40.902 --> 00:03:43.623
that the world needs
your authentic self-expression.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.658
AG: It's a liberating mantra:

00:03:46.682 --> 00:03:47.863
"Be yourself.

00:03:47.887 --> 00:03:50.000
Don't worry about what
everyone else thinks."

00:03:50.024 --> 00:03:52.986
Recorded speaker 4:
This push for authenticity is awesome.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:56.118
Recorded speaker 5: I'm being authentic.
I did not rehearse this.

00:03:56.142 --> 00:03:58.536
You're about to get
18 minutes of me unplugged.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.266
AG: So what exactly is authenticity?